<section>

    <h2>Project Overview</h2>

    <p>
        This project shows how I improved a prompt step by step,
        making the instructions clearer and more specific at each stage.
    </p>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Baseline – Weak Prompt</h2>

        <p><strong>Prompt:</strong> Write a LinkedIn post about AI.</p>

        <p>
            The result was general. I needed a clearer goal and a more specific
            direction.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Version 1 – Clear Goal</h2>

        <p>
            I changed the prompt to explain how AI helps students learn
            more effectively.
        </p>

        <p>
            The response became more focused on education, but it was still
            too general.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Version 2 – Audience</h2>

        <p>
            I specified university students as the audience.
        </p>

        <p>
            The examples became more relevant to students, but the prompt
            still lacked personal context.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Version 3 – Context</h2>

        <p>
            I added my experience in the FlyRank AI Fluency Internship.
        </p>

        <p>
            This made the post more personal and believable, although it
            became a little too long.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Version 4 – Output Format</h2>

        <p>
            I asked for three short paragraphs.
        </p>

        <p>
            The result became easier to read, but the tone was still
            somewhat formal.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Version 5 – Quality Criteria</h2>

        <p>
            I added a word limit and asked for an engaging tone.
        </p>

        <p>
            The final result became shorter and more engaging.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Final Reusable Prompt</h2>

        <p>
            Write a LinkedIn post explaining how AI helps university students
            learn more effectively. Base the post on an AI Fluency Internship
            experience. Use three short paragraphs, keep it under 150 words,
            use a natural and engaging tone, and end with a question that
            encourages discussion.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
        <h2>Lessons Learned</h2>

        <p>
            I learned that a strong prompt can be built gradually by adding
            a clear goal, audience, context, output format, and quality criteria.
        </p>
    </div>

